{"title":"The Nested Sum Theorem","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><p><b>WARNING:</b> This theorem is created by an untrustworthy person and is NOT verified. A mistake is very possible, and if you found it, please correct it as soon as you can.\n</p><p><i>This theorem is both <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">The Nested Sum Theorem</a> and <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=The_Lattice_Point_Theorem\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"The Lattice Point Theorem\">The Lattice Point Theorem</a>, so both pages redirect here.</i>\n</p><p>The <b>Nested Sum Theorem</b> (otherwise known equivalently as the <b>Lattice Point Theorem</b>) is a theorem in <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Number_Theory\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Number Theory\">Number Theory</a> that describes the relation between <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Nested_sums\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Nested sums\">nested sums</a> and <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Combinatorics\" title=\"Combinatorics\">Combinatorics</a>.\n</p>\n<div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Statement\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Statement</span></a>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Nested_Sum_Theorem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1.1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Nested Sum Theorem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Lattice_Point_Theorem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1.2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Lattice Point Theorem</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Proof\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Proof</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Applications\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Applications</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Practice_Problems\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Practice Problems</span></a>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Introductory\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4.1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Introductory</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#Intermediate\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4.2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Intermediate</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-9\"><a href=\"#Olympiad\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4.3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Olympiad</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-10\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Statement\">Statement</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=The_Nested_Sum_Theorem&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Statement\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>There are two forms of this theorem, both obviously equivalent.\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Nested_Sum_Theorem\">Nested Sum Theorem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=The_Nested_Sum_Theorem&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Nested Sum Theorem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> be a arbitrary positive integer. Then,\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/5/f/95f8d9ccdd6d7a339fe3ae148c979da1ef396583.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\sum_{x_{k-1}=1}^{x_{k}} (\\sum_{x_{k-2}=1}^{x_{k-1}} ( \\dots \\sum_{x_{1}=1}^{x_{2}} (\\sum_{x=1}^{x_{1}} 1 )) \\dots )) = \\dbinom{x_{k}+k-1}{k}\\]\" width=\"392\" height=\"54\" />\n</p><p>, where there is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> nested sums.\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Lattice_Point_Theorem\">Lattice Point Theorem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=The_Nested_Sum_Theorem&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Lattice Point Theorem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> be an arbitrary positive integer. Then the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> dimensional region\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/2/d/22d05083cb32ede2d5ba53b646ce9bdd7f8896d3.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[E= \\{ (x, x_1, x_2, \\dots , x_{k-1}) | 1 \\le x \\le x_1 \\le x_2 \\le \\dots \\le x_{k-1} \\le x_k \\}\\]\" width=\"488\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p>contain <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/4/5/d4532ff8861a8e1c57433edab1b98d8a2bce9326.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\dbinom{x_{k}+k-1}{k}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -23px\" width=\"112\" height=\"55\" /> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Lattice_points\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Lattice points\">lattice points</a>.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Proof\">Proof</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=The_Nested_Sum_Theorem&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Proof\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We proceed by induction. \n</p><p>The base case, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/e/d/5ed8470bc717a49aafe4556c7e2c2e11ddc7b687.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"42\" height=\"13\" /> is obvious, since\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/8/f589786a5ae10b03ae9b3585aa36fab6889f51ca.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\sum_{i=1}^{n} (1) = n= \\dbinom{n}{1}\\]\" width=\"142\" height=\"53\" />\n</p><p>Suppose the theorem holds for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" />, so that \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/5/f/95f8d9ccdd6d7a339fe3ae148c979da1ef396583.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\sum_{x_{k-1}=1}^{x_{k}} (\\sum_{x_{k-2}=1}^{x_{k-1}} ( \\dots \\sum_{x_{1}=1}^{x_{2}} (\\sum_{x=1}^{x_{1}} 1 )) \\dots )) = \\dbinom{x_{k}+k-1}{k}\\]\" width=\"392\" height=\"54\" />\n</p><p>where there is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> summations.\n</p><p>Then, \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/e/2/7e2cc72b180af74a561912c7db3675547b8a1298.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\sum_{x_{k}=1}^{x_{k+1}} (\\sum_{x_{k-1}=1}^{x_{k}} ( \\dots \\sum_{x_{1}=1}^{x_{2}} (\\sum_{x=1}^{x_{1}} 1 )) \\dots )) = \\sum_{x_{k}=1}^{x_{k+1}} (\\dbinom{x_{k}+k-1}{k})\\]\" width=\"425\" height=\"54\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/a/2/aa25e1c5a9eb958043965af3de6f7d6129766a30.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[=\\dbinom{x_{k+1}+k}{k+1}\\]\" width=\"110\" height=\"53\" />\n</p><p>by the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Hockey_Stick_Identity\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Hockey Stick Identity\">Hockey Stick Identity</a>.\n</p><p>The result follow from induction.\n</p><p>The lattice point form of the theorem is obviously equivalent. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/6/c/b6cf65b1f2fbdf388e3daeff9b96b34d3399d777.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\square$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Applications\">Applications</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=The_Nested_Sum_Theorem&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Applications\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>This theorem in its different forms is very useful. The summation form is useful for algebra. The lattice point form is useful for geometry involving lattice points. Another interpretation of the theorem is that for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Distinguishability\" title=\"Distinguishability\">indistinguishable</a> objects, the number of ways to put it into <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> available spaces in a specific order is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/f/b/5fba07cda033877b4c5ff5ed738b23f417a39434.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\dbinom{n+k-1}{k}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -23px\" width=\"104\" height=\"55\" />. This interpretation is important for <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Combinatorics\" title=\"Combinatorics\">Combinatorics</a>.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Practice_Problems\">Practice Problems</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=The_Nested_Sum_Theorem&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Practice Problems\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Introductory\">Introductory</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=The_Nested_Sum_Theorem&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Introductory\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Intermediate\">Intermediate</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=The_Nested_Sum_Theorem&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: Intermediate\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<ul><li>Suppose there is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" /> hats and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> bins to put them in, and all objects are assigned a corresponding integer. Suppose there is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> ways of putting the hats in the bins such that the following criteria are followed:</li></ul>\n<p>(i) If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/c/8/4c8b76bca5358138116d4d962e20e582bfa708b2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$i&lt;j$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"41\" height=\"17\" /> (where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/8/34857b3ba74ce5cd8607f3ebd23e9015908ada71.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"8\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/2/8122aa89ea6e80784c6513d22787ad86e36ad0cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$j$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"10\" height=\"17\" /> are integers), then hat <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/8/34857b3ba74ce5cd8607f3ebd23e9015908ada71.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"8\" height=\"14\" /> is placed in a bin whose number is less than or equal to the number of the bin that hat <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/2/8122aa89ea6e80784c6513d22787ad86e36ad0cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$j$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"10\" height=\"17\" /> is placed in\n</p><p>(ii) There is at least one bin that contains at least two hats\n</p><p>Find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/f/6/6f6c448f70857d76e4d88b9398140958abe1497e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x \\mod 1000$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"102\" height=\"14\" />. (<a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Number_Theory_Problems_Collection&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"Number Theory Problems Collection (page does not exist)\">Source</a>)\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Olympiad\">Olympiad</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=The_Nested_Sum_Theorem&amp;action=edit&amp;section=9\" title=\"Edit section: Olympiad\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=The_Nested_Sum_Theorem&amp;action=edit&amp;section=10\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Number_Theory_Problems_Collection&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"Number Theory Problems Collection (page does not exist)\">Number Theory Problems Collection</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Hockey_Stick_Identity\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Hockey Stick Identity\">Hockey Stick Identity</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Combinatorics\" title=\"Combinatorics\">Combinatorics</a></li></ul>\n<p><i>This article is a stub.  Help us out by <span class=\"plainlinks\"><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=The_Nested_Sum_Theorem&amp;action=edit\">expanding it</a></span>.</i>\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018112006\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.028 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.048 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 181/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 307/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 4/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 5162/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    6.426      1 Template:Stub\n100.00%    6.426      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:30461:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261018112006 and revision id 248404. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}